# Armstrong Number is a number that equals the sum of its own digits each raised to the power of the total number of digits. For example, \(153\) is an Armstrong number because it has 3 digits, and \(1^3 + 5^3 + 3^3 = 1 + 125 + 27 = 153\).
num = int(input("Enter number: "))  # Get input from user and convert it to an integer
sum = 0                             # Create a variable to hold the running total sum
temp = num                          # Copy the original number to use in our loop

while temp > 0:                     # Keep looping until all digits are chopped away
    digit = temp % 10               # Get the last digit of the current number
    sum = sum + digit ** 3          # Cube the digit and add it to the sum total
    temp = temp // 10               # Remove the last digit from the number

if num == sum:                      # Check if the final sum matches the original number
    print("Armstrong Number")       # Print success message if they are exactly equal
else:                               # Run this block if the numbers do not match
    print("Not Armstrong Number")   # Print failure message if they are not equal

